WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.707
People need to know what they should do,

00:00:01.707 --> 00:00:02.880
and one of the things they should do

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.300
is take responsibility.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.180
Have you heard of

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.600
Jordan Peterson?

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:11.140
He’s a psychologist who lectures about responsibility.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.610
­­­
I assumed that would bore young people, yet

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.460
millions watch his videos,

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.856
and buy his book.

00:00:16.856 --> 00:00:20.140
12 Rules is unbelievably successful.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.520
Number one on Amazon,

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.460
t­­­hat almost never happens with non-fiction.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.100
Yeah.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.980
Well, it's also a difficult book.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.760
It's a dark book as well.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.060
It's not the sort of thing

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.760
that you would expect people to line up to buy.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.800
And yet they do...

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.300
they line up...

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.420
IN long lines.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.960
Excited, says Peterson

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.300
to learn about responsibility.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.692
Young men get excited

00:00:43.692 --> 00:00:46.460
when you talk to them about responsibility?

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.700
Yeah, fancy that, eh?

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:49.910
Who would have ever guessed that?

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:50.900
I wouldn't have.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:51.660
No, no kidding.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.460
No kidding.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.140
Emergence of ethical behavior.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.960
When Peterson first rented a lecture hall, he

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.720
didn’t know if anyone would listen to him speak.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.480
Can you imagine this, eh?

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.199
As an invitation to a lecture.

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:05.489
Okay, we're gonna talk about the old testament

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:06.570
in a really dark way.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.790
It's like you think that's gonna be successful?

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.830
And we're gonna talk about responsibility and truth.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.260
Oh, they'll be beating down the doors

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.640
to attend those lectures.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.830
And they all sold out.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.980
His lectures continue selling out,

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.320
because, he says,

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:23.360
People have been fed this diet of pabulum,

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.070
rights, and impulsive freedom.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.220
Free tuition.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:29.160
Making quality childcare affordable.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.220
You have a right to a living wage.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:33.240
All we've had for sixty years is a dialogue

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.290
about rights.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:36.960
There's just an absolute starvation

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.960
for the other side of the story.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.590
Well, that leaves a hole in people's hearts.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:43.420
Peterson fills that hole with

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:44.660
things he learned from his

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:47.280
clinical psychology practice.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.545
It's in responsibility that most people find

00:01:49.545 --> 00:01:50.200
the meaning

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.460
that sustains them through life.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.040
It's not in happiness.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.740
It's not in impulsive pleasure.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.073
Instead, he says,

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.840
the way to find meaning is:

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:02.220
to adopt the responsibility for your own well-being,

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.280
and to try to put your family together, and

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:05.900
to try to serve your community,

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.580
and to try to seek for eternal truths and to live them.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.660
That's the sort of thing

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.940
that can ground you in your life

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.880
enough, so that you can withstand the difficulty of life.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.320
Research backs him up.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.000
People feel fulfilled

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.800
when they feel competent.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.220
It's very helpful for people to hear

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:22.920
that they should make themselves competent,

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.420
and dangerous, and take their proper place in the world.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:28.060
Competent, and dangerous.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.460
Why dangerous?

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:31.080
There's nothing to you otherwise.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.640
If you're not a formidable force,

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.620
there's no morality in your self-control.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.380
If you're incapable of violence,

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.396
not being violent isn't a virtue.

00:02:39.396 --> 00:02:42.070
People who teach martial arts know this full well,

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.070
right?

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:43.975
If you learn a martial art

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:44.940
you learn to be dangerous,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.260
but simultaneously you learn to control it.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.330
It's the alternative to being weak.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.020
Naive, and weak, and harmless,

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.691
which is what young men are being encouraged to be.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.460
Encouraged, says Peterson by

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:58.020
educators and media that bash masculinity.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.422
The problem is toxic masculinity.

00:03:00.422 --> 00:03:01.660
Toxic masculinity.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.860
Toxic masculinity.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.540
You're alienating young men.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.220
We're telling them that they're patriarchal oppressors.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.160
That's a bad message, says Peterson.

00:03:09.168 --> 00:03:10.880
Life is a very difficult process.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.760
You’re not prepared for it unless

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.510
you have the capacity to be dangerous.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:18.960
By dangerous, that implies I should be

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.220
ready to threaten someone, to hurt somebody.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.127
No, you should be capable of it,

00:03:24.127 --> 00:03:27.760
but that doesn't mean you should use it.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.760
Your female critics say,

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.730
you men are already stronger than we.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.700
You abuse us, and you're encouraging that.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.300
Oh, well,

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.758
that's definitely not the case.

00:03:38.758 --> 00:03:42.960
But lots of people call Peterson sexist, transphobic,

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.990
evil.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.560
From Vox,

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:49.578
you've claimed feminists have an unconscious wish

00:03:49.578 --> 00:03:51.530
for brutal male domination.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.660
You tell me why they line up with the Islamists?

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:55.680
Not all do.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.710
They just haven't criticized them.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:00.460
Well, that's good enough for me.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.888
You'd think if the feminists

00:04:01.888 --> 00:04:03.470
practiced what they'd preached,

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:05.182
there'd be non-stop demonstrations

00:04:05.182 --> 00:04:06.240
against Saudi Arabia.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.330
Saudi women -- They still cannot get married,

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.420
travel abroad, or open a bank account without

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.320
permission of a male guardian.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.620
You see how much concern there is

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.540
among the radical feminists for the rights of women.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:19.040
Others dismiss him as shallow.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.010
Articles call him a charlatan.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:23.540
“The stupid man’s smart person”?

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.620
Peddling fascist mysticism

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.960
because comments like

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.290
“toughen up, you weasel”

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.170
and “compassion is a vice”

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.340
provide “philosophical backup" to

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.317
demagogues like Donald Trump.

00:04:35.317 --> 00:04:36.540
He’s fired!

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.670
Compassion is a vice?

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.090
If it's taken too far.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.650
Hyper-protectiveness.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.220
Helicopter parenting.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.000
All of that.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:44.860
When you have children,

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.978
you have to encourage them to take risks

00:04:46.978 --> 00:04:48.180
because they have to grow up,

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.250
and take their place in the world.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.720
You can't protect them too much

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.240
